Interactive render delegate edits of a shader imager graph through a UsdImagingGL.Engine, from python

A red sphere is rendered with the imager graph of an ArnoldNodeGraph, set by the arnold:global:imager render setting.
The exposure of its root imager is edited, before and during the render, an imager_color_correct is inserted as its
input (before it in the chain) and removed, the root imager is replaced by an imager_shader whose flat shader is edited
during the render, and the imager setting is cleared. Covers the fixes of the imager updates (#2758, #2764). The render
delegate is driven by a headless UsdImagingGL.Engine as a viewport does, see
testsuite/common/interactive_engine_test.py. Each render is checked in test.py. There is no reference image yet: it is
to be added from a first run with a python USD, the last render being compared against it from then on. Edits that
aren't rendered correctly yet are reported as warnings (known issues in test.py).

author: sebastien.blaineau.ortega@autodesk.com

PARAMS: {'script': '"{}" test.py'.format(usd_python)}
